  about:{kicker:'About Tarmem', title:'A platform that makes renovation clear from start to finish', p1:'Tarmem is a Saudi platform that brings the homeowner and the contractor together in one place, from the first description of a project to its handover. You start by describing what you want done in your home, and bids arrive from verified contractors in your city and in the trade you need, which you compare on price, duration, licences and past work. Once you choose your contractor, everything between you stays in one place: what you agreed, the messages, the photos of each stage, and the status of every payment.', p2:'Renovating a home is one of the largest decisions an owner makes. A significant sum, work that runs for weeks or months inside their home, and a contractor they usually know only through a number passed on by a relative or an advertisement. That is where the familiar problems begin: a price that changes after work starts, a duration that stretches with no clear reason, and a verbal agreement the two sides read differently when payment falls due.', p2b:'We built Tarmem to turn all of that into something written and clear. That you know who you are dealing with before you begin, that the agreement is detailed rather than spoken, that you can see where the work has reached without asking, and that you know in advance what happens if you disagree. Clarity here serves both sides: the homeowner knows where their money goes, and a serious contractor finds someone who values their work and pays on time without delay.', p3:'Tarmem is an intermediary platform, not a contractor. Delivery, its responsibility and its quality rest with the contractor you choose. Our role is to verify contractors’ identity and licences before they appear on the platform, to organise payments so that no stage is released until you approve it, to keep the full project record for both sides to return to when needed, and to support you if a disagreement arises so it is settled by what is recorded rather than what each side remembers.', missionK:'Mission', mission:'That an owner renovates their home with peace of mind, knowing who they are dealing with and where their money goes. And that a serious contractor finds real opportunities, organised work, and payment that arrives on time.', visionK:'Vision', vision:'For Tarmem to become the first reference for renovation work in the region, and for clarity in price, agreement and handover to become what this sector expects rather than the exception.', growthK:'Where we are going', growth:'We begin in Saudi Arabia, then the UAE and Kuwait. As the core process proves itself we build on it: a stronger mobile experience, services for suppliers, partnerships with developers, and options for renovation financing.', partnersTitle:'Partner network', partners:['Real estate developers','Interior designers','Material suppliers','Payment providers','Banks and financing','Property professionals']},
  faq:{kicker:'Questions', title:'Frequently asked', more:'Didn’t find your answer?', contact:'Contact support', items:[{q:'What does a “verified contractor” mean?',a:'A verified contractor is one whose papers we reviewed before they appeared on the platform: identity, commercial registration, licences and evidence of past work. The badge states what we checked; it does not by itself guarantee workmanship.'},{q:'How does paying by stage work?',a:'The project is split into stages, each with a clear deliverable and a set amount. The stage amount is held before it begins, the contractor uploads evidence of completion, and you review it. Your approval releases that stage’s payment.'},{q:'How much does Tarmem charge?',a:'Homeowners pay 5% of the agreed project value, and contractors pay 10% deducted from stage payments. Posting, bidding and comparing carry no fees.'},{q:'What happens if I disagree with the contractor?',a:'Raise the disagreement against the stage in question, and each side submits its explanation and evidence. The support team reviews the project record both sides can see to reach a documented outcome. The stage payment stays held until the disagreement is settled. Anything not settled this way follows the escalation route set out in the terms and conditions.'},{q:'Do I need an ID or Iqama?',a:'Yes. Verifying your identity with a national ID or Iqama is required before posting a project or bidding.'},{q:'Do you carry out the work yourselves?',a:'No. Delivery and its responsibility rest with the contractor you choose. Our role is to verify contractors, organise payments, keep the project record, and support both sides when needed.'},{q:'Which payment methods are supported?',a:'Bank cards, mada and Apple Pay, through a licensed payment partner.'},{q:'When am I charged?',a:'The homeowner fee is added when the first stage amount is held after you agree. The contractor commission is deducted as each payment is released. You are charged nothing while you are still comparing.'},{q:'What if the project stops halfway?',a:'Released stages stand as they are, and anything not yet released is returned to you or split according to what was actually completed, under the cancellation terms.'}]},
